{"id": "EUVD-2026-86116", "enisaUuid": "93b46ca5-8690-3088-9b0f-051e117cd57c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: cfg80211: reject duplicate wiphy cipher suite entries\n\nDuplicate entries in wiphy->cipher_suites do not describe any\nadditional capability, but cfg80211 currently accepts them and leaves\nindividual consumers to deal with them.\n\nOne such consumer is the WEXT compatibility code, which appends a WEP\nkey length for each WEP cipher entry it sees. Repeated WEP entries can\ntherefore overflow the fixed iw_range::encoding_size array returned by\nSIOCGIWRANGE.\n\nReject duplicate cipher suite entries in wiphy_register() instead.\nThis keeps the cipher suite invariant in one place and makes malformed\nwiphy descriptions fail early with -EINVAL, rather than relying on a\nsingle cfg80211 user to handle duplicates correctly.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:05:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d12e92e72db914e1ea777c6f246f6be75985438e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1305f8b925fe92edf5fec183588dfc7db719180b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4cbb2360f4d8c29e67bc7a8bf6ba0ae096583923", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7187d145d9042b037e4f10538f70cf95e380219f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97518", "GHSA-q434-f3vh-rmc4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "199660ad-ff4f-337c-a072-90da8bd0c6d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "19da64b4-2fd0-372e-adb6-aedbf0e72829", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "1e6a47d6-a645-3608-9063-8d289510896e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5c677476-5546-37a2-be5a-83349c6dff4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ab658f9ce218ae93b3d2db2b3fe68bfefb81196 <1305f8b925fe92edf5fec183588dfc7db719180b"}, {"id": "6edeaea7-be04-3d73-804e-5ea1bf7151b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "842878b1-86d6-3c82-bdbe-7329f0ea09af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ab658f9ce218ae93b3d2db2b3fe68bfefb81196 <4cbb2360f4d8c29e67bc7a8bf6ba0ae096583923"}, {"id": "8d64b283-7999-3f67-832f-7cc93d98882c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cd59a687-19a0-3a7a-b98d-4c3aa405ed32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ab658f9ce218ae93b3d2db2b3fe68bfefb81196 <d12e92e72db914e1ea777c6f246f6be75985438e"}, {"id": "d09c6add-ef46-37fa-a23f-73e02940fbf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2ab658f9ce218ae93b3d2db2b3fe68bfefb81196 <7187d145d9042b037e4f10538f70cf95e380219f"}, {"id": "d8c700cf-b089-37a8-8ca1-bedf2fd954cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cb02dc51-12cb-30d1-b28f-d7f0d14e17fb", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}